# OpenCode agent frontmatter (V2 fields). The installer wraps this in frontmatter fences and appends core.md.
#
# Rules are ordered and the last match wins. `*` matches any characters including `/`; `?`
# matches exactly one character. Start from deny-all, then allow only what the agent needs.
# Nothing here allows shell, subagent, external_directory, execute, or MCP tools.
#
# Edits are an allow-list (ruling R27). OpenCode matches `edit` resources as workspace-relative
# paths (verified on 2.1.4), case-sensitively outside Windows, so the allows are exact-case and
# a differently cased path falls through to deny-all. Three denies follow the allows: a WORKING
# folder two segments below 03_TAX_YEARS (`?` also matches `/`, so `TY_????` alone would take
# `TY_a/bc/WORKING/x`; this deny cannot match the real `TY_2024/WORKING/x`), nested WORKING
# folders, and a case-blind deny shaped like STRATEGY_SEED.md (8 chars, `_`, 4, `.`, 2),
# because on a case-insensitive disk `01_STRATEGY/strategy_seed.md` is the seed and would
# otherwise match the `01_STRATEGY/*` allow. `TY_????` cannot say "digits": it approximates.
#
# Web search is denied on purpose (the explicit `websearch` deny below stays visible after the
# deny-all). OpenCode's first search asks the user to pick a search provider; a non-interactive
# `opencode run` cannot answer that question, so it is cancelled and the run exits 1. Denying it
# also keeps queries away from any third-party search service. The agent researches by fetching
# the official hosts below directly, including their site-search pages. (`websearch: false` is
# top-level config only and the installer writes no project opencode.json, hence a permission.)
#
# Web fetch is limited to exact https authority hosts, each listed twice: `https://<host>/*` for
# any path and the bare `https://<host>` (the bare URL does not match the `/*` form). A wildcard
# host (`https://*.irs.gov/*`) would be unsafe because `*` also matches `/`, so it would admit
# `https://evil/x.irs.gov/`. `http://` stays denied. State tax sites are not listed; add both
# `https://<host>/*` and `https://<host>` allows for the states you need.
description: Tax advisor for a local multi-year U.S. tax workspace. Reads the workspace, researches current law by fetching official sources, and writes analysis outside protected evidence paths.
mode: primary
permissions:
